      "answer": "For city driving, buying a used car is almost always the better financial move.\n\nA 3-5 year old used car is already depreciated, costs far less to buy, and you own it outright. City driving means stop-start traffic, parking dings, and high mileage - all things that destroy lease value and trigger expensive penalties.\n\nLease a new one only if you must have the latest safety tech and you drive under 10,000 miles per year with zero tolerance for repairs.\n\nBuy the used car. Buy it outright, keep it 10 years.",
