      "answer": "Use a hosted provider.\n\nBuild your own login system only if you have a dedicated security team and compliance requirements that forbid third-party auth. For everyone else: use a hosted provider.\n\nUse Auth0, Clerk, or AWS Cognito. One provider. One integration. Done.\n\nDo not build passwords, 2FA, password reset, breach monitoring, or social logins yourself. You will ship insecure auth.\n\nHosted provider gives you: secure password storage, breach monitoring, MFA, social logins, passwordless, compliance certifications, and support.\n\nCost of a breach > cost of provider by 100x.\n\nIf you must own auth: use open source battle-tested stack: Keycloak self-hosted. Never roll your own crypto.\n\nDecision: Hosted provider. Ship today.",
